    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a challenging slate today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who anchor our daily projections with efficiency scores of 76.04 and 74.56, respectively. Despite looming matchups against high-caliber arms like Gerrit Cole and Kyle Bradish, both players benefit significantly from favorable park factors and high-leverage spots in the projected order. **Gunnar Henderson** remains our most reliable asset against the tough arm of Cole due to his dynamic platoon advantage, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** provides a high-ceiling performance profile against Bradish. Furthermore, **Sam Antonacci** earns a \"Strong\" start with a 63.14 rating, bolstered by an excellent matchup against G. Holmes and the primary leadoff spot, making him a critical engine for run production today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished just outside the starting threshold with a 38.21 score. While his elite sprint speed makes him a high-priority asset for our stolen base-starved 5x5 build, the daunting matchup against Jacob deGrom\u2014combined with a bottom-of-the-order projection\u2014severely suppressed his scoring potential. Consequently, we are sacrificing his baserunning upside to avoid the efficiency floor. Conversely, we must maintain caution with **Coby Mayo** (46.68) and **Wade Meckler** (53.18); while they make the lineup, their scores are hovering near marginal levels. Their output is heavily tethered to the assumption of favorable batting order placements, and any movement down the lineup card could render these starts detrimental to our daily game cap management.",
